<LegalLayout 
  title="Affiliate Disclosure" 
  description="Affiliate and advertising disclosure for Bangladesh Travel Guide: how we earn commissions through CJ Affiliate and Booking.com links, how Monetag advertising works, and how this does not affect our editorial content."
  lastUpdated="October 21, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Bangladesh Travel Guide is free to read and is supported by affiliate commissions and advertising. This page explains how that works, so you can decide how to use the links on our site. It applies to every page of <a href="https://www.bangladeshtravelguide.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.bangladeshtravelguide.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Is an Affiliate Link?</h2>
  <p>
    An affiliate link is a link to a third-party company's website that contains a tracking code. If you click the link and then make a booking or purchase, the company may pay us a commission. This costs you nothing extra, and the price you pay is set by the provider, not by us.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Our Affiliate Partners</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Booking.com, through CJ Affiliate:</strong> Our destination guides include links and banners for accommodation on Booking.com. These links are provided through the CJ Affiliate network. If you book a stay after clicking, we may earn a commission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may add other travel-related partners in future, such as eSIM providers or tour operators. If we do, we will apply the same standards and update this page.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This website also displays advertisements served by Monetag, a third-party advertising network. We earn revenue from these advertisements, but we do not choose or endorse the individual ads shown, and we do not control which advertisers appear. If you see an ad you consider inappropriate or misleading, please tell us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. For how advertising technologies use data, see our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How Links Are Identified</h2>
  <p>
    Affiliate links are tagged as sponsored in the page code, using the <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute, as recommended by search engines, and they open in a new browser tab. This page is the site-wide disclosure that applies to every affiliate link and banner, whether or not a separate note appears beside it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Editorial Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Our affiliate and advertising relationships do not determine what we write. Partners do not review, approve, or pay for our guides, and they have no influence over our safety advice, risk warnings, or destination coverage. We place affiliate links where they are relevant to the topic, such as accommodation links on destination pages, and we do not hide or change risk information because a link might earn money. Where we advise against travel to an area or describe restrictions, we do so regardless of any commercial effect. Our approach is explained in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your Bookings and Third-Party Terms</h2>
  <p>
    When you click an affiliate link, you leave our website. Any booking or purchase is a contract between you and the provider, and their prices, availability, cancellation terms, and privacy practices apply. We are not a party to your booking and cannot change, cancel, or refund it. Please check the details on the provider's website before you pay. A hotel booking is not a visa or permit and does not guarantee entry to any restricted area. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for more.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this disclosure, please contact us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. You can also read more about the site in our <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
  </p>
